From 844ac922249089b87c0e88b613a97f5e4adc4d98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Lukens <jlukens@botch.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:15:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add optional RF listener support

A PLM hears only what reaches its own antenna. Battery devices (leak,
door, motion, remotes) are RF-only and can't be polled, so a message the
modem misses from one of them is lost. Receive-only RF listeners placed
elsewhere in the house (an ESPHome board with a CC1101, an RTL-SDR)
decode what they hear and publish it to MQTT; this compares what they
heard with what the modem heard and hands the modem's misses to the
protocol stack. Nothing is transmitted.

New optional `mqtt.listeners` config section. Without it nothing is
created and nothing changes. With it, Listeners:

- subscribes to decoded listener messages (default insteon-rf/msg/+):
  JSON carrying the message as the modem would have reported it
  (0x50/0x51 frame), its on-air time and receiver diagnostics;
- holds each message 2.5 s for the modem's own (often later, powerline)
  copy and does nothing if the modem heard it;
- classifies the rest into tiers (battery, group, state), never
  handling replies, the modem's own messages, unknown senders, repaired
  messages or group 0 (which raises an alert instead);
- injects listed tiers through the new Protocol.inject(), logs "shadow"
  tiers only, with per-device and global rate limits;
- publishes per-listener and per-device counters (retained) and group 0
  alerts.

Protocol gains signal_raw_read (every frame read from the modem) and
inject(), which accepts only complete 0x50/0x51 frames and ignores the
modem's own copy of an injected message for 3 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0157MSwwBp84p98F4Aq9dGR3
